      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "yes \u2014 ligand-induced surface expression preserved in response to TNF\u03b1 (EC50 = 0.057 \u00b1 0.011 nM), IL-1\u03b1, IL-1\u03b2, LPS, VEGF165a, and histamine; surface display confirmed by membrane-impermeable LgBiT complementation",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing introduced an 11-aa HiBiT tag plus a GSSG linker into the endogenous SELE locus in HUVECs and TERT2-HUVECs, placing the tag immediately after signal-peptide cleavage (after A21, before W22). Surface display was confirmed with membrane-impermeable exogenous LgBiT (NanoBiT complementation), proving the tag is extracellular. Ligand-induced expression in response to TNF\u03b1 (EC50 = 0.057 \u00b1 0.011 nM), IL-1\u03b1, IL-1\u03b2, LPS, VEGF165a, and histamine was fully preserved, confirming normal trafficking and inducible expression. No disulfide cysteines, N-glycosylation sequons, or known functional residues are disrupted at this junction. The GSSG linker provides conformational flexibility away from the lectin-domain ligand-binding surface. [validation: surface_and_function; position: inferred; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "citation": "preprint",
          "claim": "(B) General genome-editing strategy showing the PAM sequence adjacent to the signal sequence of E-selectin and the insertion of HiBiT and a GSSG linker immediately following the signal sequence in the HiBiT-tagged E-selectin sequence."
        }
